    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.0,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.15,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.97 from 6 h onward. I tested whether that plateau hides saturation by diluting the 18 h aliquot. The 10x dilution read 0.107, which scales to 1.07. The 40x dilution read 0.022, which scales to 0.88. Both scaled values sit within about 10% of the undiluted 0.97 and fall on both sides of it. They show no systematic rise with dilution. If the reader were saturating, the diluted samples would scale to well above 1. The scatter at such low OD is plausibly measurement noise. So the plateau looks like a real stationary phase at an OD of about 1.0. Each dilution had only one replicate, so the evidence is limited."
  },
